m. Let me use get_tile_at_pixel at various points. Let me instead sample the HUD at pixel level.\n\nActually, the row-3 read: col 11 = $2E, col 12 = $29, col 13 = $00, col 14 = $00, col 15 = $24. In the screenshot \"x00\" — the x at around x=112-120? Hmm. Let me just check with get_tile_at_pixel for pixel (88,26) etc. Simpler: the coin icon in SMB is drawn with sprite tiles. list_sprites would show palette-... let me check.\n\nHmm, but the task is specifically about the font and HUD layout. Let me be systematic and use get_tile_at_pixel on a few pixels to confirm mapping of nametable to screen and identify the coin.\n\nLet me think about how SMB lays out the HUD. Known SMB1 status bar:\nRow (top) at tiles y=2: \"MARIO   WORLD  TIME\"\nRow y=3: \"000000  x00  1-1   340\"\n\nActually the coin icon is at tile col 11-12? And \"x\" at col 13? Wait in real SMB the layout is:\n- MARIO at cols 3-7\n- score at cols 3-8 (row 3)\n- coin icon (sprite) around col 11\n- \"x\" background tile at col 13\n- coin count digits at cols 14-15? \n\nHmm, our read: col 11=$2E, col12=$29, col13=$00,col14=$00. If \"x\" is at col 11 ($2E) and coin count at col 12,13? No.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I mis-assumed. Let me re-examine: the coin in the screenshot looks like it's at x≈101-110, which is cols 12-13 (x 96-111). Then \"x\" at x≈114-119 (col 14), then digits \"00\" at col 15-16? But our read shows col 13,14 = $00,$00.\n\nHmm, the discrepancy suggests the coin icon is a sprite and the background tiles beneath/around differ. Let me just query.\n\nLet me get list_sprites and get_tile_at_pixel at (100,26), (110,26), (118,26), (126,26), (134,26).\n\nActually pixel y for row 3 is 24-31, use y=27.\n\nLet me also note: the HUD occupies rows 2-3 (y tiles 2 and 3) = pixel y 16-31. Rows 0-1 are blank $24.\n\nLet me now read the tiles for all identified glyph tiles. Digit tiles: $00, $01, $03, $04. Letter tiles: $16,$0A,$1B,$12,$18,$20,$15,$0D,$1D,$0E. Also need $28 (dash), $29, $2E. And possibly the coin \