{"type":"thinking","text":"The title screen confirms the same HUD rows 2-3 with the same tile IDs:\n- Row 2: cols 3-7 = 16,0A,1B,12,18 (MARIO); cols 18-22 = 20,18,1B,15,0D (WORLD); cols 25-28 = 1D,12,16,0E (TIME).\n- Row 3: cols 3-8 = 00 x6 (score 000000); col 11 = 2E (coin), col 12 = 29 (x), cols 13-14 = 00,00 (coin count); cols 19-21 = 01,28,01 (WORLD 1-1); cols 26-28 = 36,36,36 ($24 blanks) because TIME hasn't been set yet on the title screen (title screen shows blank TIME?). \n\nHmm, on the title screen row 3 cols 26-28 = $24 ($24=36) meaning blank. And the screenshot shows \"TIME\" label but no digits under it. Right — the title screen shows \"TIME\" with no number (blank). Also the score shows 000000 and coin x00 and WORLD 1-1.\n\nWait, the title screenshot shows \"MARIO 000000, coin x00, WORLD 1-1, TIME\" with no digits. Yes matches.\n\nGreat. So the HUD layout is confirmed on both title and 1-1.\n\nNow, note one nuance: on the title screen the coin icon is at col 11 too. Let me verify with get_tile_at_pixel? Not necessary; the nametable read is the same.\n\nNow I need to record:\n1. note 'HUD layout' with the rows/columns.\n2. tile mappings for the font glyphs: \n   - chr:0x100 digit 0\n   - chr:0x101 digit 1\n   - chr:0x103 digit 3\n   - chr:0x104 digit 4\n   - chr:0x116 letter M\n   - chr:0x10A letter A\n   - chr:0x11B letter R\n   - chr:0x112 letter I\n   - chr:0x118 letter O\n   - chr:0x120 letter W\n   - chr:0x115 letter L\n   - chr:0x10D letter D\n   - chr:0x11D letter T\n   - chr:0x10E letter E\n   - chr:0x128 dash\n   - chr:0x129 multiply x\n   - chr:0x12E coin icon\n\nFor each: mapping_type 'tile', id '0x100' etc (id should be the tile id; and table: 1). The instruction says \"record each with record_mapping mapping_type tile, the tile id, table, a plain name ('font digit 0', 'font letter M') and group 'font'\".\n\nThe id — \"the tile id\". Examples use id '0xB4' with table. Hmm, but for table 1, the entry is keyed chr:0x1B4. So id should be '0x16' with table 1? Or id '0x116'? Looking at existing entries: \"chr:0x145: brick top-left\" — id is '0x145' and table presumably 1. And \"0x60-0x6A: warp_pipe_tile_set (palette 0) [pipe]\".\n\nHmm, record_mapping says: \"For a tile give table so the key names the picture, not just the id.\" and table: \"Tiles: the pattern table the tile is drawn from, 0 ($0000) or 1 ($1000). The entry is then keyed chr:0x1B4\".\n\nSo if id='0x16', table=1 → keyed chr:0x116. That seems the intent: the id is the nametable tile id, and table disambiguates. But the existing entry \"chr:0x145\" used id='0x145' perhaps. Hmm. Actually the existing chr:0x145 entry id is \"0x145\" and it says nametable tile id $45. So they recorded id as the chr value? Ambiguous.\n\nTo be safe and unambiguous, I'll use id = the nametable tile id (e.g. '0x16') with table 1, so the resulting key would be chr:0x116. Hmm, but if the tool prefixes 'chr:0x1' + id... Let me think. The tool description: \"table: ... The entry is then keyed chr:0x1B4\". For id '0xB4' and table 1 → chr:0x1B4. That matches the chr:0x1B4 example. So id should be the nametable tile id (0xB4), table 1, and the key becomes chr:0x1B4.\n\nBut the existing \"chr:0x145\" entry would then have id '0x45' table 1. The displayed key is chr:0x145. OK.\n\nSo for M (nametable $16, table 1): id='0x16', table=1, key chr:0x116.\n\nHmm, but wait: the task says \"the tile id, table\". Given SMB BG pattern table is $1000, the tile id $16 with table 1. I'll provide id '0x16' and table 1. To be extra clear I'll mention CHR $116 in notes/name? The name is 'font letter M'. Hmm, but if the tool key is chr:0x116, good.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Existing entries: \"0x60-0x6A: warp_pipe_tile_set\" has no table field (it spans two tables?). And \"chr:0x153: question_block_16x16_metatile\". Hmm chr:0x153 means id '0x53' table 1. And \"chr:0x145\"→ id '0x45'. So yes, id = nametable tile id, table = 1.\n\nFor the coin $2E → id '0x2E', table 1 → chr:0x12E. \n\nNow, also I should record the HUD note with id 'HUD layout'. mapping_type 'note', name 'HUD layout'.\n\nLet me write the note carefully:\n\n\"HUD layout (status bar), nametable 0 rows 0-3 (pixels y0-31), BG pattern table $1000:\n- Rows 0-1 all blank tile $24.\n- Row 2 = labels (all BG palette 2, white): 'MARIO' cols 3-7 (tiles $16 $0A $1B $12 $18 = M,A,R,I,O); 'WORLD' cols 18-22 (tiles $20 $18 $1B $15 $0D = W,O,R,L,D); 'TIME' cols 25-28 (tiles $1D $12 $16 $0E = T,I,M,E).\n- Row 3 = values: score 6 digits cols 3-8 (tile $00 = 0 each); coin icon col 11 (tile $2E, BG palette 3, orange coin); multiply sign col 12 (tile $29 = x, palette 2); coin count 2 digits cols 13-14 (tile $00); world number cols 19-21 = world digit, dash ($28), level digit (in 1-1: $01 $28 $01 = '1-1'); TIME 3 digits cols 26-28 (in 1-1 e.g. $03 $04 $00 = 340).\n- Verified by read_nametable 0 (0,0) 32x4 plus screenshots on the title screen and in World 1-1; both show the same tiles.\"\n\nAlso mention the coin is a background tile not a sprite: there IS an OAM sprite at x=88 tile $FF palette 7, but rendered coin pixels (x90,y28 = $27 orange) come from background tile $2E palette 3 (get_region object at (91,28) CHR 0x12E, slots 1,3).\n\nActually, the sprite $FF at x=88 y=25 does draw a few pixels (rows 30-31) but its tile is mostly blank. Hmm, its pixels are at x89-93, y30-31. It might be a leftover sprite. I'll note the coin is the BG tile $2E.\n\nHmm, wait, but the sprite at x=88 palette 7 with tile $FF... In SMB, the coin icon in the HUD IS a sprite! Let me reconsider. Actually get_region at (91,28) returned background palette 3 slots [1,3] with CHR 0x12E — it's the background. And get_pixel_color(90,28) = $27 orange. Both agree that the pixel at (90,28) is background tile $2E palette 3.\n\nBut actually wait — get_region pixel_count 31, box (89,24)-(93,30), CHR 0x12E. And read_tile(302) shows an 8x8 coin shape with index 1 fill and index 3 shading. So the coin = tile $2E (CHR $12E). Good. The sprite $FF is a separate partial thing — maybe an artifact of the pause. I'll not emphasize it.\n\nHmm, but actually the coin in the HUD is animated (pulsing) in SMB1? Let me not worry.\n\nNow, also I should record the blank tile $24? Not required.\n\nLet me now record all these mappings. That's 17 tile mappings + 1 note = 18 record_mapping calls. Plus promote_mappings at the end.\n\nLet me batch them in a few parallel groups. record_mapping calls are independent, so I can do many in one message.\n\nLet me construct each:\n\n1. note: id 'HUD layout', name 'HUD layout', mapping_type 'note'\n2. tile: id '0x00', name 'font digit 0', group 'font', table 1, confidence 1\n3. tile: id '0x01', name 'font digit 1', group 'font', table 1\n4. tile: id '0x03', name 'font digit 3', group 'font', table 1\n5. tile: id '0x04', name 'font digit 4', group 'font', table 1\n6. tile: id '0x16', name 'font letter M', group 'font', table 1\n7. tile: id '0x0A', name 'font letter A', group 'font', table 1\n8. tile: id '0x1B', name 'font letter R', group 'font', table 1\n9. tile: id '0x12', name 'font letter I', group 'font', table 1\n10. tile: id '0x18', name 'font letter O', group 'font', table 1\n11. tile: id '0x20', name 'font letter W', group 'font', table 1\n12. tile: id '0x15', name 'font letter L', group 'font', table 1\n13. tile: id '0x0D', name 'font letter D', group 'font', table 1\n14. tile: id '0x1D', name 'font letter T', group 'font', table 1\n15. tile: id '0x0E', name 'font letter E', group 'font', table 1\n16. tile: id '0x28', name 'font dash / hyphen', group 'font', table 1\n17. tile: id '0x29', name 'font multiply sign x', group 'font', table 1\n18. tile: id '0x2E', name 'HUD coin icon', group 'font'? Hmm the coin isn't a font glyph. The task says record font tiles; the coin is part of HUD. I could record it as group 'hud' or 'font'. Better group 'hud' or 'coin'. I'll use group 'hud' maybe, or 'hud_coin'. Actually the task says \"the font: read_tile on the digit tiles and on the letters the status bar uses ... record each with ... group 'font'\". The coin/dash/x aren't letters/digits. I'll record dash and x as font (they're status-bar glyphs) and the coin as a separate group 'hud'.\n\nHmm, dash $28 and x $29 — the task said \"digit tiles and letters the status bar uses\". The dash and x are neither. But including","truncated":true}
