{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_0Gbn9Hc3LCRz7YGlNung1698","tool":"record_mapping","input":{"mapping_type":"note","id":"HUD layout","name":"HUD layout","confidence":1,"notes":"Status bar of Super Mario Bros. (World): fixed at the top of nametable 0, tile rows 2-3 (y pixels 16-31). Rows 0-1 are blank tile $24 (CHR $124). All glyphs are background tiles from BG pattern table $1000, drawn with BG palette 2 (slot 1 = $30 white); tiles are named by nametable id (chr = id + $100).\nLABELS Row 2 (tile_y=2): 'MARIO' cols 3-7 ($16 $0A $1B $12 $18 = M A R I O); 'WORLD' cols 18-22 ($20 $18 $1B $15 $0D = W O R L D); 'TIME' cols 25-28 ($1D $12 $16 $0E = T I M E).\nVALUES Row 3 (tile_y=3): score = SIX digits at cols 3-8 (under MARIO); coin icon = col 11 (tile $2E / CHR $12E, BG palette 3 because its attribute block is 3, slots 1 $27 orange + 3 $0F black); multiply sign 'x' = col 12 (tile $29 / CHR $129); coin count = TWO digits at cols 13-14; world/level digits = cols 19-21, i.e. world digit, dash $28, level digit (World 1-1 displays $01 $28 $01); TIME = THREE digits at cols 26-28.\nPROOF: read_nametable 0 (x0,y0) 32x4 gives exactly this, and screenshots on the title screen and in World 1-1 match. In World 1-1 the status bar read MARIO 000000, coin x00, WORLD 1-1, TIME 335/340/357; on the title screen it reads the same labels with score 000000, coin x00, WORLD 1-1, and the three TIME digit cells left blank ($24). The coin at col 11 is a BACKGROUND tile, not the OAM sprite near it: get_region object mode at (91,28) returned 31 connected pixels of background palette 3, box (89,24)-(93,30), CHR 0x12E, and get_pixel_color(90,28) read $27 orange; get_tile_at_pixel(90,28) returned tile_id 46 ($2E) chr_tile 302 ($12E), palette 3. Scroll is 0 over the HUD (get_tile_at_pixel scroll_x=0 at every HUD pixel), so the bar stays put while the playfield scrolls."}}
