{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's the mapping sheet for the SMB status bar.\n\n## HUD layout (nametable 0, tile rows 2–3)\n\nEverything is drawn from BG pattern table `$1000` with BG palette 2 (white `$30`); tile rows 0–1 are blank `$24`. Verified by `read_nametable 0 (0,0) 32×4` plus screenshots on **both** the title screen and World 1-1.\n\n| Element | Row | Columns | Tiles |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `MARIO` | 2 | 3–7 | `$16 $0A $1B $12 $18` |\n| `WORLD` | 2 | 18–22 | `$20 $18 $1B $15 $0D` |\n| `TIME` | 2 | 25–28 | `$1D $12 $16 $0E` |\n| score (6 digits) | 3 | 3–8 | `$00 ×6` |\n| coin icon | 3 | 11 | `$2E` (palette 3, `$27` orange) |\n| `x` | 3 | 12 | `$29` |\n| coin count (2 digits) | 3 | 13–14 | `$00 $00` |\n| world/level | 3 | 19–21 | `$01 $28 $01` = `1-1` |\n| `TIME` digits (3) | 3 | 26–28 | e.g. `$03 $04 $00` = `340` |\n\nTitle screen reads the same labels/score/coin/WORLD 1-1, but leaves the three TIME digit cells blank (`$24`).\n\n## Font tiles (BG table `$1000`, group `font`)\n\n- **Digits:** `$100`=0, `$101`=1, `$103`=3, `$104`=4\n- **Letters:** `$116`=M, `$10A`=A, `$11B`=R, `$112`=I, `$118`=O, `$120`=W, `$115`=L, `$10D`=D, `$11D`=T, `$10E`=E\n- **Symbols:** `$128`=dash (`-` in 1-1), `$129`=`x` (multiply sign)\n- **HUD icon (group `hud`):** `$12E` = coin, drawn by background tile `$2E` at col 11, palette 3 (confirmed with `get_region` object mode at (91,28): 31 background palette-3 pixels, CHR `0x12E`).\n\n## Reach confirmation\n`$0770` stayed 1 through the Start/wait/Start sequence (the game was already in a level, so Start paused/unpaused), and the screenshot showed `WORLD 1-1` with the HUD live. A reset then reproduced the identical bar on the title screen.\n\n## Recorded\n1 layout note (`HUD layout`) + 17 tile mappings. `promote_mappings` saved all 18 (confidence 1) into the ROM mapping file — now 40 tiles / 7 palettes / 26 addresses. No ROM bytes were written."}
